    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>In 589 Sui troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiankang">Jiankang</a> and the last Chen emperor surrendered, ending the Northern and Southern dynasties period and reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> proper.</li><li>The Sui built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal</a>, extended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-wall-of-china">Great Wall</a> and rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> as a planned capital, conscripting millions of workers at a heavy human cost.</li><li>Four expeditions against Goguryeo all failed by 614, and the dynasty disintegrated amid revolts that ended with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-yang-of-sui">Emperor Yang</a>'s assassination in 618.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Sui army massed against Goguryeo was so large that the histories record it took 30 days for all its units to leave their rallying point near Shanhaiguan, and it stretched over about 410 kilometres.</p></aside>
    </section>

